// i18n — Carino Branding. Fleet convention (see Hardware/i18n.js, Compass/i18n.js):
// the English source strings ARE the keys, so a missing entry falls back to
// English and there is no 'en' block. carino-lang.js (deferred, loaded just
// before this script) owns the language preference and fires 'carino:langchange';
// this file owns the dictionaries and re-applies on every switch.
//
// Static markup uses data-i18n (textContent), data-i18n-html (innerHTML, for the
// leaves that carry inline <b>/<code>/<a> formatting) and data-i18n-title (the
// title attribute). Strings the page script builds at runtime go through the
// TT() bridge in index.html -> window.t.
//
// Deliberately NOT translated: design-token names (--fs-*, --accent), CSS class
// and selector names (.cs-btn, .modal-rack), font families (IBM Plex Sans, Red
// Hat Display), code samples, product/repo names (Carino PACS, Topo, Stocks) and
// the type-scale step tags that label those tokens.

